# Windows desktop development settings. Electron does not load this file automatically.
# Export the values in your shell before `npm start`; do not put credentials in this file.
# The production app uses https://sipper.dev and the public OAuth client sipper-windows.
# It has no client secret. Tokens and managed SIP settings use OS-encrypted local storage.
# Managed message alerts need no extra provider settings. They are a separate,
# default-off app preference, poll only while Sipper runs and show no message text/names.
# Clicks refresh current customer access; quitting, opt-out and known withdrawal clear notices.
# Actual Windows toast delivery/clicks and packaged DPAPI still need Windows verification.

# Optional separate app-data directory. Set an absolute path for isolated development.
# Example on Windows: C:\Users\YourName\AppData\Local\SipperDevelopment
# Example on macOS: /tmp/sipper-windows-development
SIPPER_DATA_DIR=

# Optional development server origin. Honoured only by unpackaged apps with SIPPER_DATA_DIR.
# HTTPS is required except for explicitly isolated localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1] development.
# Use http://localhost:3100 alongside the local portal. The portal must have the
# sipper-windows OAuth client and sipper://oauth/callback redirect registered.
# Development copies do not take over the operating system's sipper:// association.
SIPPER_MANAGED_SERVER=https://sipper.dev

# Set to memory only for disposable development profiles. Managed session storage also
# requires SIPPER_DATA_DIR before using this mode. Nothing survives closing the app.
# Leave unset for production-equivalent OS encryption. No plaintext storage fallback exists.
SIPPER_TEST_PASSWORDS=

# Set to 1 for silent tests with no microphone/speaker access.
SIPPER_NULL_AUDIO=

# Optional custom engine executable; ignored by packaged apps.
SIPPER_ENGINE=

# Optional Sipper application log mirror to stderr. Logs can describe calling activity;
# do not publish real-account diagnostic output or test with production PBX credentials.
SIPPER_LOG_STDERR=

# Optional real gateway integration on a Mac. Set in the portal/ shell, not the installed app:
# SIPPER_WINDOWS_GATEWAY=1 node --import tsx --env-file-if-exists=.env scripts/gateway-smoke.ts
# Requires the isolated gateway prerequisites in gateway/README.md. Uses fictional users,
# null audio and a private temporary CA; never set this against a production database/PBX.
# SIPPER_TEST_GATEWAY_FILE is generated and removed by that harness. Do not create it yourself.
# Windows runtime tests require an engine built with build-windows.ps1 -Testing; rebuild
# without -Testing before creating an installer. Production engines omit all test hooks.

# Real local portal acceptance on macOS: run pnpm test:windows-portal from portal/.
# Requires the built Windows C engine, built portal, local PostgreSQL and Mailpit.
# Uses its own disposable database, fictional SIP registrar and in-memory token store.
# SIPPER_TEST_PORTAL_FILE is generated/removed by the harness; do not set it yourself.
# Browser gestures, Windows DPAPI/Schannel and audible media need separate acceptance.
# Optional shared directory status uses the same management origin and no extra key.
# Requires portal migration 030; sharing is controlled in the portal and defaults off.

# Managed messaging uses this same origin, OAuth identity and enrolled device.
# Apply portal migrations 032 and 033 before upgrading Windows/Apple clients. No new key.
# Independent page expiry is at most 30 seconds, foreground polling every 5 seconds.
# Bodies, drafts and retry IDs stay in memory and are excluded from session storage.
# Owner-managed groups: 20 people; messages: 4096 UTF-16 code units. Retention is server-owned
# SIPPER_MESSAGE_RETENTION_DAYS (see portal/.env.example), not a desktop setting.
# test:windows-portal includes real direct/group sends, nonce retries, peer replies,
# shared read state and suspension. Its consent/storage remain test boundaries.
# Generic running-app chat alerts are implemented locally. Actual Windows/Electron
# IPC, toast display/clicks and production acceptance remain unverified.

# Hosted meetings use this same management origin and enrolled device, with no
# desktop API secret. Apply portal migration 036 and the current meeting API first.
# The portal returns a short-lived grant for the separate Sipper media window;
# grants and retry IDs stay in memory and never enter the managed session file.
# Configure the five server-only settings in portal/.env.example plus the private
# SFU and Sipper signalling proxy described in docs/MEETINGS.md. Leaving those
# settings empty shows meetings unavailable; it does not prevent managed calling.
# Production media signalling requires WSS. Insecure WS is accepted only for the
# explicitly isolated loopback development profile described above.
# Meeting capture starts off and needs explicit permission/source selection.
# SIPPER_NULL_AUDIO affects the SIP test engine, not browser meeting capture.
# Electron-on-Mac generated-video tests do not prove Windows permissions, DPAPI,
# installer contents, physical audio/video or coordination with active SIP calls.
